1. Executive Summary
Midnight at BMSIT is a cartoon-style browser escape game set in a fictional, spooky version of BMSIT. The player is a student who stays late to finish a project and accidentally becomes locked inside the campus after midnight. The lights go out, doors become locked, strange sounds echo through the buildings and goofy cartoon zombies begin wandering around.
The player must explore different campus-inspired areas, find objects, collect clues, solve puzzles, avoid zombies and environmental obstacles, restore power and unlock the main gate before the countdown ends. The game should be funny and suspenseful rather than graphic or genuinely frightening.
The project will be built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript. A simple point-and-click structure is recommended so that the project remains achievable without Unity, Unreal Engine, a server or a database.
2. Product Vision, Goals and Non-Goals
2.1 Vision
Create a small but memorable cartoon escape adventure that feels like an indie browser game and uses a familiar college setting, humorous characters, interactive scenes and puzzle-solving.
2.2 Goals
Create a complete beginning-to-ending game experience.
Use a fictionalized BMSIT campus setting that feels familiar without claiming to reproduce the exact campus layout.
Include multiple rooms, interactive objects, inventory, clues, puzzles, zombies and obstacles.
Make controls simple enough for first-time players.
Support desktop and mobile browser interaction.
Demonstrate DOM manipulation, events, conditions, arrays/objects, timers, CSS animation and LocalStorage.
2.3 Non-Goals for the First Version
No 3D world, multiplayer networking or online accounts.
No real-time voice chat, camera or microphone features.
No complex enemy pathfinding or physics engine.
No real campus security information, real room access details or exact building maps.
No graphic violence, blood or realistic weapons.
