4. Story, Setting and Tone
4.1 Story Introduction
The player is a BMSIT student who stays late on campus to finish a mini-project. At midnight, the power suddenly fails. The main gate is locked, the phone has no signal and the campus announcement system crackles to life: “Attention, night owl. Please proceed to the exit. And please do not feed the zombies.” The player discovers that strange cartoon zombies are roaming the campus. To escape, the student must restore power, collect two access-card fragments and solve the gate code.
4.2 Tone and Visual Boundaries
Use playful spooky visuals, expressive cartoon faces and exaggerated reactions.
Zombies should be goofy, slow or silly—not realistic or graphic.
Use harmless hiding, distraction and timing mechanics instead of combat.
Use fictional room names and a stylized campus layout.
Clearly present the zombie outbreak as fictional game storytelling, not a real BMSIT event.
5. Main Gameplay Loop
1.Enter a campus area and inspect the scene.
2.Tap or click highlighted objects to read descriptions or discover clues.
3.Collect useful items in the inventory.
4.Solve the room puzzle or activate a mechanism.
5.Avoid or distract zombies and handle environmental obstacles.
6.Unlock the next area and continue toward the main gate.
7.Combine the required items, enter the final code and escape.
Core system	Purpose
Exploration	Discover clues and interact with room objects.
Inventory	Store keys, notes, fuses and access-card pieces.
Puzzles	Require observation, logic, sequence memory or item use.
Zombie AI	Create tension using patrol, alert and chase/approach states.
Hazards	Make the player consider noise, timing and route choices.
Timer and score	Encourage replay and faster completion.

6. Level-by-Level Game Design
Level 0 – Opening Sequence
Scene: A cartoon title screen showing the campus at night, moonlight, a flickering lamp and a tiny zombie silhouette behind a tree.
Display game title and tagline.
Buttons: Play, How to Play, Sound On/Off and Credits.
Show a short comic panel explaining why the student is still on campus.
Start the countdown only when the player enters the first playable scene.
Level 1 – Classroom Block
Objective: Find the classroom key and decode a clue to unlock the corridor.
Element	Details
Scene objects	Teacher's desk, blackboard, school bag, cupboard, wall clock, scattered books and door.
Items to find	Small torch, folded note and classroom key.
Puzzle	A three-digit code is hidden in a blackboard clue. The player inspects the board and enters the code on the desk drawer.
Zombie	Zombie Student: slowly patrols the corridor and reacts to noisy actions.
Obstacle	Loose books: clicking or stepping near them increases the noise meter.
Exit condition	Open the desk drawer, collect the key and unlock the corridor door.
Comedy moment	A note says: “If found, please return this key. The attendance shortage is already serious.”

Level 2 – Library
Objective: Find a fuse and the first access-card fragment.
Element	Details
Scene objects	Bookshelves, reading table, librarian desk, computer, archive cabinet and wall lamp.
Items to find	Fuse, torn campus map and access-card fragment A.
Puzzle	Arrange three marked books in the order suggested by a note or shelf symbols.
Zombie	Zombie Librarian: investigates sound and moves between two shelf positions.
Obstacle	Rolling library ladder blocks the direct route; wait for it to move or use another hotspot.
Exit condition	Solve the book-order puzzle, open the archive cabinet and collect the fuse and card fragment.
Comedy moment	The zombie librarian makes a “Shhh!” speech bubble when the noise meter rises.

Level 3 – Canteen
Objective: Distract the zombie chef, restore part of the power system and find access-card fragment B.
Element	Details
Scene objects	Serving counter, tables, fridge, food tray, menu board, kitchen door and power switch.
Items to find	Plastic tray, power switch key and access-card fragment B.
Puzzle	Repeat a short sequence of food icons or coloured buttons shown by a clue on the menu board.
Zombie	Zombie Chef: guards the serving counter and reacts to movement or noise.
Obstacle	Spilled juice slows the player for a few seconds; a moving trolley periodically blocks the corridor.
Exit condition	Use the tray as a harmless distraction, solve the sequence and activate the power switch.
Comedy moment	The zombie chef chases the smell of an imaginary midnight dosa.

Final Level – Main Corridor and Gate
Objective: Combine the access-card fragments, enter the final code and escape.
Element	Details
Scene objects	Security desk, gate control panel, emergency light, locked main gate and corridor noticeboard.
Required items	Access-card fragment A, access-card fragment B and the final code clue.
Puzzle	Combine the card fragments, inspect the clue and enter the correct code on the gate panel.
Zombie	Gatekeeper Zombie: patrols between the security desk and gate.
Obstacle	A short power outage disables the gate panel until the fuse has been installed.
Exit condition	Restore power, enter the code while the route is clear and activate the gate.
Ending	Show the student escaping at sunrise with a humorous final message.

