7.1 Simple Enemy State Model
State	What happens	Example trigger
Idle	Zombie waits or performs a looping animation.	No player noise nearby.
Patrol	Zombie moves between two or three predefined points.	Normal gameplay timer.
Alert	Zombie turns toward the source and displays an alert icon.	Player triggers a noisy object.
Approach	Zombie moves a short distance toward the alert location.	Noise meter reaches a threshold.
Reset	Zombie returns to patrol after a short delay.	Player hides or waits.

Beginner implementation: use JavaScript timers and a small number of predefined positions. A full navigation or pathfinding algorithm is not needed.
8. Obstacles and Hazard Rules
Hazard	Effect on player	Rule / response
Loose books	Raises noise and may alert the zombie student.	Avoid the book pile or accept the noise penalty.
Slippery juice	Temporarily slows movement or delays an action.	Wait for the slip effect to end.
Flickering lights	Some objects are hard to see.	Find and use the torch to reveal clues.
Locked doors	Block access to a new room.	Find the matching key or solve the code.
Power failure	Disables the final gate panel.	Find and install the fuse.
Moving trolley	Blocks the corridor at intervals.	Wait for a safe gap before proceeding.
Noise meter	At a high level, zombies become alert.	Avoid noisy interactions or use a safe hiding spot.

Fairness rule: Hazards should warn the player before a major consequence. The game should not punish a player with an unavoidable instant failure.
9. Puzzle Specifications and Example Solutions
Puzzle	Clue	Player action	Example solution / result
Classroom drawer code	Blackboard shows three simple symbols with a number clue.	Inspect board and enter three digits.	Correct code opens drawer and reveals the classroom key.
Library book order	A note says: “Start with the oldest, then the blue cover, then the smallest.”	Select three marked books in order.	Correct order opens archive cabinet.
Power fuse	Fuse box label shows an empty slot and a matching fuse symbol.	Select fuse from inventory, then select fuse box.	Lights and gate panel power are restored.
Canteen sequence	Menu board shows a sequence of food icons.	Repeat the sequence using on-screen buttons.	Correct sequence opens kitchen compartment.
Final gate code	Two card fragments and a noticeboard clue reveal the code.	Combine fragments and enter code.	Gate opens and victory sequence starts.

Important: The actual numeric codes and sequence should be set in the JavaScript game data. The examples above are design guidance; the development team can choose final values and ensure that all clues lead consistently to them.
