11. Game Rules, Timer and Scoring
11.1 Timer
Suggested default duration: 12 minutes for the full first version.
The timer begins when Level 1 starts, not on the title screen.
Pause stops the timer and pauses active zombie movement.
When time reaches zero, show the Game Over screen and offer Retry.
Difficulty settings may change the timer: Chill 15 minutes, Standard 12 minutes, Spooky 9 minutes.
11.2 Noise Meter
Noise starts at zero.
Selected actions add noise, such as knocking over books or dropping an object.
At a warning threshold, show a visual alert and zombie reaction.
At a high threshold, trigger a short approach/chase event.
Noise may decrease slowly while the player remains in a safe location.
11.3 Scoring
Action	Suggested score
Complete a room	+100 points
Solve a puzzle without a hint	+50 points
Collect an optional hidden sticker	+25 points
Use a hint	−10 points
Trigger a noise alert	−15 points
Escape with time remaining	Bonus based on remaining time

Final rank examples: Campus Legend, Night Owl, Almost Caught, Zombie's Favourite Student. These ranks are humorous labels, not real academic results.
