22. Final Project Description
Midnight at BMSIT is a 2D cartoon horror-comedy escape game developed using HTML, CSS and JavaScript. Set in a fictionalized version of BMSIT after midnight, the game challenges a student to explore campus areas, collect objects, solve puzzles, avoid goofy cartoon zombies and overcome environmental obstacles. The player must restore power, assemble access-card fragments and unlock the main gate before time runs out. The project demonstrates front-end programming, interactive UI design, game-state management, event handling, timers, animations, responsive design and browser-based data storage.
23. Short Abstract for Project Submission
Midnight at BMSIT is a browser-based 2D escape adventure designed as a basic web development project. The game places the player in a fictional cartoon version of BMSIT after midnight, where they must escape from a locked campus while avoiding cartoon zombies and environmental obstacles. Players explore different locations, collect items, solve interactive puzzles and unlock routes to the main gate. The system is developed using HTML5, CSS3 and JavaScript, with optional use of the Canvas API and LocalStorage. The project combines entertainment with practical implementation of front-end web technologies, interactive event handling, animations, timers and game-state management.